<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Pedro Álvares Cabral</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1500</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Pedro Álvares Cabral was a Portuguese navigator who reached the coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a> in 1500 while leading a fleet to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>. His landfall gave Portugal a claim to Brazil. Brazil became the most durable territorial possession of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/pedro-alvares-cabral.jpg" alt="Pedro Álvares Cabral" width="284" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Aurélio de Figueiredo · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Pedro_%C3%81lvares_Cabral.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
